  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q22-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "Find the units digit of $7^{7^7}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$3$\n\nThe units digits repeat every four powers, and $7^7\\equiv3\\pmod4$.",
      "worked": "The units digits of successive powers of $7$ are $7,9,3,1$, repeating every four powers.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}7^7&\\equiv(-1)^7\\pmod4\\\\7^7&\\equiv-1\\pmod4\\\\7^7&\\equiv3\\pmod4\\end{align*}$$\n\nWrite $7^7=4k+3$ for an integer $k$. Since $7^4\\equiv1\\pmod{10}$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}7^{7^7}&=7^{4k+3}\\\\7^{7^7}&=(7^4)^k\\times7^3\\\\7^{7^7}&\\equiv1^k\\times343\\pmod{10}\\\\7^{7^7}&\\equiv3\\pmod{10}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe units digit is $3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
